WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:11.437
A gradual rollout is optional for larger fleets. Health gates
run when you approve checks; each batch needs explicit operator
advancement. This example leaves the plan paused.

2
00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:14.525
Choose Rollouts to plan a release in stages.

3
00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:20.103
Create a gradual rollout. Choose the release and the matching
device platform.

4
00:00:20.690 --> 00:00:26.365
A cohort is simply a batch. Add devices or groups; a device
belongs to only one batch.

5
00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:33.242
Choose the pacing, observation period and failure threshold.
Creating the plan does not start devices.

6
00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:42.810
Select the rollout and waiting devices. Check device health and
continue requires wallet approval. Admission does not prove a
device is online.

7
00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:52.199
Devices are still waiting here. After admission, signed post-
apply health and observation gates control progression when you
approve further checks.

8
00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:59.893
Pause stops new admissions. It does not undo an update already
allowed to start; this example admits no devices.

9
00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:08.383
The plan is paused. Resume when ready, then explicitly approve
checks and each later batch. Closing the browser stops
coordination.

10
00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:17.269
This plan is saved and paused; no devices were admitted.
Automatic health gates do not replace your explicit approvals
for further progress.
